@startuml
title Applying a wireless audio configuration

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "Control application" as Client
participant "GATT service" as Gatt
participant "Protocol decoder" as Protocol
participant "Configuration manager" as Manager
database "Persistent settings" as Settings
participant "Bluetooth host" as Host
participant "Bluetooth peer" as Peer

Client -> Gatt: Enable response indications
Client -> Gatt: Write configuration_command\n(request_id, set_*, persist)
Gatt -> Protocol: Decode command

alt Payload is malformed
    Protocol --> Gatt: Decode error
    Gatt --> Client: ATT error\n(no protocol response)
else Payload is well formed
    Protocol --> Gatt: Typed command
    Gatt --> Client: ATT write response
    Gatt -> Manager: Validate and apply command

    alt Value or section is unsupported
        Manager --> Gatt: command_result(unsupported or invalid)
        Gatt -> Client: Indicate configuration_response\n(same request_id)
        Client --> Gatt: Confirmation
    else Command is accepted
        opt persist = 1
            Manager -> Settings: Store validated section
            Settings --> Manager: Stored
        end

        alt Can be applied to the current connection or stream
            Manager -> Host: Request ACL, codec, or QoS update
            Manager --> Gatt: command_result(pending)
            Gatt -> Client: Indicate configuration_response\n(same request_id)
            Client --> Gatt: Confirmation
            Host -> Peer: Bluetooth update procedure
            Peer --> Host: Accepted, negotiated, or rejected
            Host --> Manager: Effective parameters / status
            Manager -> Gatt: Publish runtime_state
            Gatt -> Client: Notify effective state
        else Reconnect or stream restart is required
            Manager --> Gatt: command_result(restart required, section mask)
            Gatt -> Client: Indicate configuration_response\n(same request_id)
            Client --> Gatt: Confirmation
        end
    end
end

note over Client,Peer
The command result reports acceptance of the requested configuration.
runtime_state reports the parameters that actually became effective.
end note
@enduml
